  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "R2 studies the same W-Ta-Cr-V BCC alloy using a DFT-fitted cluster expansion and Monte Carlo sampling, providing a related surrogate-model intervention and direct evidence for chemical short-range ordering. R4 and R10 further establish temperature-dependent SRO in the closely related W-Ta-Cr-V-Hf system, while several other records provide only broad support for ordering or electronic/thermodynamic contributions to phase stability. None describes an MTP for the liquid, FEP as a replacement for thermodynamic integration, matching of the DFT phase-space distribution, or variance-controlled MTP-to-DFT free-energy corrections. Thus the records point toward the importance of SRO and efficient fitted models, but the combined MTP/FEP melting-point methodology would still require a substantial new idea."
